      "writtenOn": "2025-08-25T18:44:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "mBindings is slab allocated with [SlabAllocator](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/common/SlabAllocator.h;l\u003d192?q\u003dSlabAllocato\u0026sq\u003d) to be in the [same allocation as the BindGroup](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/BindGroupLayoutInternal.h;drc\u003d48f660fbabd7ec824f280cbdf7f33dac87ef37dc;l\u003d170). It directly follows it in the allocation. I could make it an std::optional but it would bloat the normal bindgroups for now reason (`DynamicArrayState` is expected to grow a bunch) so it would be nice to keep it separate, though if it were an `std::optional` it would still require a single branch to skip it in the destructor.",
